  "question": {
    "text": "Given below are two statements :<br />Statement (I) : Alcohols are formed when alkyl chlorides are treated with aqueous potassium hydroxide by elimination reaction.<br />Statement (II) : In alcoholic potassium hydroxide, alkyl chlorides form alkenes by abstracting the hydrogen from the $\\beta$-carbon.<br />In the light of the above statements, choose the most appropriate answer from the options given below :",
    "image": null
  },
